  "interactionBehavior": {
    "summary": "Text is presentational by default: a `<span>` with no hover, press, or focus styles, no click handler, and no tab stop. Copy is selectable — `user-select` is not suppressed. `as=\"a\"` plus `href` forwards `href` / `target` / `rel` onto a native anchor, but OneUI still paints `text-decoration: none` and does not add a hover colour, a focus halo, or `cursor: pointer`; pass `underline` if the link should look like a link, and rely on the browser's native outline for keyboard focus. `maxLines` clamps with an ellipsis and does not set `title`, so truncated copy has no hover tooltip. `tabIndex` and `aria-hidden` are passthroughs only — a focusable node in the `link` slot stays in the tab order even if the root is `aria-hidden`."
  },
